{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2861af9a73966356710244eddb70a4f66935eca474db9f6aff03cfaf8fe6acc5","digest":{"component_or_area":"opcert service worker lifecycle","key_entities":["src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py","test_matching_guard_is_accepted","asyncio.wait_for","asyncio.timeout","asyncio.to_thread","queue.get","TestClient","_worker","CPython issue 86296"],"problem_keywords":["asyncio","cancellation","python 3.11","xdist worker crash","hang","wait_for","lifespan teardown","race condition"],"propositions":["Python 3.11 asyncio.wait_for can consume an external cancellation when its child future completes in the same turn, causing the opcert worker to loop back to queue.get() with a pending cancellation count","TestClient teardown cancels the opcert worker lifespan but lifespan awaits the worker forever because the cancellation was consumed, causing the hang guard to kill the xdist worker","Replacing asyncio.wait_for with asyncio.timeout semantics in src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py:76-83 preserves external cancellation and per-job timeout while fixing the Python 3.11 race","A regression oracle test must be held out and validated RED before the fix and GREEN after it on Python 3.11 to prove the defect and remediation"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787707116889380001,"uuid":"0234e96f-b07c-4257-9bd1-4eb55827a2c9"}